      "writtenOn": "2016-10-05T00:02:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Consider a weak_ptr\u003c\u003e instead. \n\n(A shared_ptr is useful if the referenced object must be kept alive. A weak_ptr is useful when we just need to know whether or not the referenced object is still around. From the code so far, it seems like WifiChip just wants to know whether or not the HAL is still around.)",
